  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason focuses on the presence of a sure outcome in each lottery. Lottery A offers 2400 Euros with 100% probability, which is a sure outcome. Lottery B offers 2500 Euros with 33%, 2400 Euros with 66%, and 0 Euros with 1% — none of its outcomes are certain. Therefore, only Lottery A has a sure outcome. The decision reason would prefer Lottery A because it is the only one with a sure outcome.",
